e biden into the  white house bloomberg is spending as  much as a hundred million dollars on  biden's campaign in florida  recent polls show trump and biden are  neck and neck in the sunshine state  voters there can start mailing in  ballots at the end of the month  still ahead as the pandemic continues  another country heads back  into lockdown  you're watching global national  a freak sandstorm darkened midday skies  near turkey's capital  a time lapse shared by the city's mayor  shows massive  dust clouds engulfing nearby buildings  officials say six people were injured  by the strong a winds thousand  protesters gathered in the capital of  belarus today in one of the biggest  demonstrations  yet demanding the country's longtime  ruler quit  [Music]  anger is not letting up protests have  been sweeping the country  since last month's contentious election  handed alexander lukashenko a landslide  victory  and a sixth term in office thousands of  people have been detained  at least three people have been killed  and hundreds hurt  as police break up the crowds the  opposition claims the vote was rigged  and key figures have since been jailed  or fled the country  israel's government is reimposing a  covet-19 lockdown  to contain a surge in cases the  three-week shutdown will start friday  which is the start of the jewish holiday  season  people will have to stay within 500  meters of their homes except to go to  work  and exercise schools restaurants and  non-essential shops will be closed  the decision has divided the nation  grappling with recession  israel is the first country to order a  second nationwide lockdown  up next the remarkable life of  indigenous advocate  nelly carlson  [Music]  montrealers did their part today to help  those who most need it by leaving  non-perishable items on their doorsteps  for food banks to collect  food banks across the country have seen  an increased demand  since the pandemic started there are  some causes that are too great